{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All new code will be written in Go to match the existing Hyperledger Fabric implementation language and toolchain.",
    "The Solo orderer (U4) will use a single goroutine reading from a buffered Go channel to emulate the batch/block creation step; no Raft/BFT consensus is required.",
    "The Solo orderer's history ledger will be implemented as an in-memory append-only structure exposing a seek/cursor API over gRPC; persistence is explicitly out of scope for this increment.",
    "The lifecycle system chaincode (U2) will be deployed as a system chaincode on a channel, storing deployment policies in its own state; policies will be expressed using the existing Fabric policy DSL.",
    "The CLI extraction (U8) will be a stand-alone binary communicating with peer nodes exclusively through the existing gRPC/protobuf interfaces; the binary will be distributed as a platform-specific (Linux/macOS/Windows) release artifact and will not link RocksDB or peer internal packages.",
    "The state cache (U6) will be implemented as an in-memory LRU layer in front of the existing peer state DB (versioned key store) and exposed via an internal Go interface consumed by the endorser to assemble read-write sets without additional I/O.",
    "Friendly chaincode names (U1) will be stored as part of the chaincode install/package metadata and resolved by the peer during instantiation, with no on-chain state changes.",
    "The GitHub mirror (U5) will be implemented via an automated CI job (Jenkins/GitHub Actions) that mirrors Gerrit changes on every merged commit; no code is forked, only mirrored read-only.",
    "Documentation (U3, U7) will be authored in AsciiDoc/Markdown and published through the unified hyperledger.org docs site; upgrade-flow docs will include a worked end-to-end example.",
    "A single integration test suite will validate all eight features end-to-end against a local network composed of peer + Solo orderer."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One experienced developer familiar with the Hyperledger Fabric code base performs all work (no hand-off overhead).",
    "The existing peer, orderer, and gRPC infrastructure is stable and does not need significant rework beyond the described changes.",
    "CI/CD infrastructure for GitHub mirroring (U5) already exists or is provided as platform-level; only the mirror configuration job is in scope.",
    "Hyperledger.org documentation hosting (U7) is provided by the Hyperledger community; the effort covers authoring, restructuring, and submission.",
    "No breaking changes to public APIs are introduced unless explicitly required by a user story (e.g., U4 introduces a new orderer type).",
    "Effort estimates cover design, implementation, unit tests, and developer-level integration tests; community/CI infrastructure provisioning is excluded.",
    "Effort is measured in productive work-hours (8 h/day) and excludes meetings, code review wait time, and unrelated maintenance."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Chaincode friendly name support (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Add a 'name' field to the chaincode install/package metadata, extend the peer CLI/SDK to set and resolve friendly names, update lifecycle and debug logs to display the name instead of/in addition to the hash. Includes unit tests and CLI usage docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Lifecycle system chaincode for deployment policies (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a new system chaincode (lscc extension) that stores and enforces per-chaincode deployment policies (endorsement, validation, collection membership). Includes policy schema, chaincode APIs (deploy, update, query), endorsement integration, and tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 70
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Upgrade flow documentation (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Author end-to-end documentation describing chaincode upgrade flows: prerequisites, CLI/SDK invocation, endorsement handling, policy updates from U2, rollback guidance, and a worked example. Submit to the Fabric docs repository.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Solo orderer implementation (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the 'Solo' orderer: a single-process orderer that ingests broadcast requests via a buffered channel, batches them into blocks on a single goroutine, and serves them through a gRPC deliver service backed by an in-RAM history ledger with seek/cursor support for reconnecting clients. Includes unit and integration tests, configuration, and operational notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 100
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "GitHub mirror of Fabric source (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Configure an automated CI job that mirrors the Gerrit-hosted Fabric repositories to a public GitHub organization on every merged change. Includes repository creation, mirror job definition, verification of ref/tag sync, and documentation of the mirror process.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "State cache for read-write set building (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement an in-memory LRU state cache layer in front of the peer state DB. Expose an interface used by the endorser to populate read sets and detect write-set conflicts without additional I/O. Includes cache invalidation on commits/rollbacks, metrics, and integration tests showing performance and correctness.",
      "most_likely_effort": 50
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Unified documentation site (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Restructure and migrate Fabric developer documentation (chaincode, application, SDK, operations) so it is discoverable from hyperledger.org. Reorganize content, update navigation, add cross-links to the upgrade-flow docs from A3, and validate build/publish pipeline.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Peer CLI extraction into standalone binary (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the peer CLI out of the validating-peer package into a separate module that depends only on public Fabric gRPC/protobuf interfaces. Produce platform-specific binaries (Linux/macOS/Windows) that no longer require RocksDB or peer internals. Update build, packaging, and install instructions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 60
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing of full increment",
      "activity_description": "Build and run an end-to-end test network (peer + Solo orderer) that exercises U1 friendly names, U2 lifecycle policies, U6 state cache, and the new CLI binary from U8. Include regression suite for chaincode deploy/upgrade, rw-set correctness with cache, and Solo orderer disconnect/reconnect scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 30
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Release notes, cleanup, and final review",
      "activity_description": "Final code cleanup, removal of dead code, updating CHANGELOG/release notes for all eight user stories, and preparing a single cohesive pull request / RFC for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 15
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 391
  }
}
```

